{
  "id": "m3l2",
  "title": {
    "es": "Diccionarios",
    "en": "Dictionaries"
  },
  "theory": {
    "es": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Pares clave -> valor"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "Un **diccionario** asocia claves con valores, entre llaves `{}`. En lugar de acceder por posición (como las listas), accedes por clave. Es ideal para representar 'fichas' de datos."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "persona = {'nombre': 'Ana', 'edad': 25}",
          "print(persona['nombre'])"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "Ana"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Añadir y modificar"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "Asignar a una clave nueva la crea; asignar a una existente la cambia."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "persona = {'nombre': 'Ana'}",
          "persona['edad'] = 25",
          "persona['nombre'] = 'Bea'",
          "print(persona)"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "{'nombre': 'Bea', 'edad': 25}"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "note",
        "value": "Acceder a una clave que no existe con `dic['x']` da `KeyError`. Para evitarlo usa `dic.get('x')`, que devuelve `None` (o un valor por defecto) si no está."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "persona = {'nombre': 'Ana'}",
          "print(persona.get('edad', 0))"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "0"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Recorrer un diccionario"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "`.keys()` da las claves, `.values()` los valores y `.items()` los pares. Recorrer el diccionario directamente itera sobre las claves."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "notas = {'mates': 8, 'lengua': 6}",
          "for asignatura, nota in notas.items():",
          "    print(asignatura, nota)"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "mates 8",
          "lengua 6"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "Comprobar si una clave existe es directo con `in`: `'mates' in notas` vale `True`."
      }
    ],
    "en": [
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Key -> value pairs"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "A **dictionary** maps keys to values, between braces `{}`. Instead of accessing by position (like lists), you access by key. Great for representing data 'records'."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "person = {'name': 'Ana', 'age': 25}",
          "print(person['name'])"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "Ana"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Adding and updating"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "Assigning to a new key creates it; assigning to an existing one changes it."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "person = {'name': 'Ana'}",
          "person['age'] = 25",
          "person['name'] = 'Bea'",
          "print(person)"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "{'name': 'Bea', 'age': 25}"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "note",
        "value": "Accessing a missing key with `d['x']` raises `KeyError`. To avoid it use `d.get('x')`, which returns `None` (or a default) if absent."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "person = {'name': 'Ana'}",
          "print(person.get('age', 0))"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "0"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "value": "Iterating a dictionary"
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "`.keys()` gives the keys, `.values()` the values and `.items()` the pairs. Iterating the dictionary directly loops over its keys."
      },
      {
        "type": "code",
        "value": [
          "grades = {'math': 8, 'lang': 6}",
          "for subject, grade in grades.items():",
          "    print(subject, grade)"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "output",
        "value": [
          "math 8",
          "lang 6"
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "text",
        "value": "Checking if a key exists is direct with `in`: `'math' in grades` is `True`."
      }
    ]
  },
  "exercises": [
    {
      "id": "m3l2e1",
      "prompt": {
        "es": "Define `contar_palabras(texto)` que devuelva un diccionario {palabra: nº de veces}. Las palabras se separan por espacios. Ejemplo: `'a a b'` -> `{'a': 2, 'b': 1}`.",
        "en": "Define `contar_palabras(texto)` returning a dict {word: count}. Words are separated by spaces. Example: `'a a b'` -> `{'a': 2, 'b': 1}`."
      },
      "starter_code": [
        "def contar_palabras(texto):",
        "    conteo = {}",
        "    # usa texto.split() y .get()",
        "    return conteo"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "def contar_palabras(texto):",
        "    conteo = {}",
        "    for palabra in texto.split():",
        "        conteo[palabra] = conteo.get(palabra, 0) + 1",
        "    return conteo"
      ],
      "hints": {
        "es": [
          "texto.split() devuelve la lista de palabras.",
          "conteo[p] = conteo.get(p, 0) + 1 suma sin fallar la primera vez."
        ],
        "en": [
          "texto.split() returns the list of words.",
          "conteo[p] = conteo.get(p, 0) + 1 counts safely the first time."
        ]
      },
      "tests": [
        {
          "type": "function",
          "name": "contar_palabras",
          "function": "contar_palabras",
          "cases": [
            {
              "args": [
                "a a b"
              ],
              "expected": {
                "a": 2,
                "b": 1
              }
            },
            {
              "args": [
                ""
              ],
              "expected": {}
            },
            {
              "args": [
                "hola hola hola"
              ],
              "expected": {
                "hola": 3
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "m3l2e2",
      "prompt": {
        "es": "Define `invertir_dict(d)` que devuelva un nuevo diccionario con claves y valores intercambiados (los valores son textos). Ejemplo: `{'a': 'x'}` -> `{'x': 'a'}`.",
        "en": "Define `invertir_dict(d)` returning a new dict with keys and values swapped (values are text). Example: `{'a': 'x'}` -> `{'x': 'a'}`."
      },
      "starter_code": [
        "def invertir_dict(d):",
        "    resultado = {}",
        "    return resultado"
      ],
      "solution": [
        "def invertir_dict(d):",
        "    resultado = {}",
        "    for clave, valor in d.items():",
        "        resultado[valor] = clave",
        "    return resultado"
      ],
      "hints": {
        "es": [
          "Recorre con .items() para tener clave y valor.",
          "resultado[valor] = clave"
        ],
        "en": [
          "Loop with .items() to get key and value.",
          "resultado[valor] = clave"
        ]
      },
      "tests": [
        {
          "type": "function",
          "name": "invertir_dict",
          "function": "invertir_dict",
          "cases": [
            {
              "args": [
                {
                  "a": "x",
                  "b": "y"
                }
              ],
              "expected": {
                "x": "a",
                "y": "b"
              }
            },
            {
              "args": [
                {
                  "k": "v"
                }
              ],
              "expected": {
                "v": "k"
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}